      "message": "Thanks @beckysiegel@google.com that\u0027s super helpful feedback. Definitely too much for a single patch anyway, but even more so with the indexing changes.\n\nI\u0027ve broken this apart and pushed it up as a 5 stack change with hashtag threaded-change-list, hopefully in a more palatable and self-contained sequence.\n\nI removed the hack for dealing with a server that doesn\u0027t have the preference. Turns out that\u0027s actually. not needed in the pure typescript version (a server will quite happily store and return a preference object it doesn\u0027t know about, which is maybe mildly concerning but we can\u0027t really come up with an real attack vector.\n\nTopic grouping is at the end separately. I love the different workflows we see in different communities. In my world use of topic is an outlier only used in specific circumstances given the semantics of \"submit together\", and that\u0027s what\u0027s driving my desire to have it clarified in the UI as-such. But I\u0027ll admit I haven\u0027t thought deeply yet about all of the topic+thread edge cases you pointed out, mostly just split that out so it\u0027s properly a separate thought.",
